<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Thymbra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/546-bce">546 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Thymbra was fought in 546 BCE in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croesus">Croesus of Lydia</a>. Cyrus then captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardis">Sardis</a> and brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionia">Ionian Greek</a> cities of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> coast under Persian rule. The victory was a key step in the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-thymbra.jpg" alt="Battle of Thymbra" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Walter Hutchinson 1877 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Defeat_of_Croesus_546_BCE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
